  "report": "Initial stage, as preserved in the supplied prior findings: distinct TikTok accounts praised packaging aesthetics in one brand-owned video thread. P00’s chic/environmentally friendly statement had 296 displayed likes; P15’s intended container reuse had 150. These support resonance, not verified environmental performance or buying effects. Environmental claims remained unresolved: P01 is brand agreement, P03 is P00’s qualified explanation, and P02 questions recyclability. P06 alone reported arrival leakage and a loose top, with 12 likes. P07 offered a replacement and asserted that short oxygen exposure was not an issue; neither shipment nor independent safety verification was established. Initial counts were arrival_leak 1, explicit_loose_top 1, bare_arrival_agreement 0, replacement_offered 1, replacement_sent 0, retailer_leak 0, and repurchase_intended 0.\n\nUpdated stage: arrival leakage now recurs across seven distinct visible TikTok accounts in the same reply branch: P06, P08–P13. P06 and P13 explicitly describe a loose/improperly screwed top; P08 adds an order from Sephora and a free replacement reportedly sent. P09–P12 supply only terse contextual agreement. They support arrival-leak recurrence at that shared level, without independently supplying the parent’s cleaning, oxygen concern, loose-top detail, or remedy. This is distinct-account repetition within one conversation, not seven verified independent humans or events. P13 supplies detailed corroboration of leakage accompanying an unsecured top, even with zero likes. The added replies have 5, 4, 4, 2, 0, and 0 likes respectively; those values do not count experiences or establish prevalence. Complaint SKU/version remains unknown.\n\nR01 adds a retailer review specifically about Softwear–Void: its lid repeatedly unscrews, including leakage in a pocket at work onto underwear, shirt, and jeans; product is lost and cannot be returned to the package. This supports leakage associated with cap loosening across community-comment and retailer-review roles at a broad level, subject to unresolved cross-venue actor overlap. It does not corroborate arrival leakage, the same SKU, or a shared manufacturing cause. R01’s account is detailed but individually scoped: 3-star rating, would_recommend=true, native verified-buyer=true, rewarded=false; engagement is unavailable. Suggested click-lock or doe-foot packaging is a customer remedy proposal, not an implemented fix. The customer’s manufacturer attribution is also unverified.\n\nConsequences: P07’s conditional brand replacement offer remains distinct from P08’s customer report of a free replacement sent; delivery is unconfirmed, and these concern different customer accounts. R01 explicitly intends to repurchase despite annoyance, loss, and price concern because they love the product and Void is their favorite. This is loyalty alongside complaint, not completed repurchase or evidence that packaging attracts purchases. P17’s all-Experiment routine and Continuum in transit show brand loyalty without packaging attribution. P20 expresses buying enthusiasm; P32 tentative saving interest; P38 trial intent; P42 receipt and newly discovered refillability. P04/P27 request refill bundles, P29 asks about a refill sticker, and P15 intends reuse. These do not establish packaging-caused purchase or additional explicit future repeat-purchase intent.\n\nReception is mixed across aesthetic approval and functional complaints; praise does not contradict or resolve leakage. Environmental performance remains unverified, and no population defect rate, causal mechanism, formula safety finding, or packaging-driven buying effect is established. The updated evidence changes the initial isolated arrival complaint into same-thread distinct-account recurrence and adds a reported shipment, a differently scoped retailer failure, and explicit repurchase intent. Initial findings were available as the supplied summary; original earlier records were not re-retrieved. No context-only accounts were supplied. TikTok observations were captured 2026-09-09T11:56:25.935Z; displayed dates lack years. Coverage remains bounded to 47 displayed bodies versus 72 advertised comments, with selected branches expanded and no native comment IDs. Counts below are updated focal source-account/record counts, not origin or event counts; P00/P03 and P01/P07 each share an actor.",
